 "post": {
  "title": "6 Signs You Think Everyone's Watching You #shorts",
  "description": "Send this to the friend who checked all six. Replaying a tiny mistake for days, mirror checks, rehearsing a coffee order: that's the spotlight effect, the feeling that everyone notices you far more than they do. In Gilovich, Medvec & Savitsky's 2000 study (Journal of Personality and Social Psychology), Cornell students wore an embarrassing T-shirt into a room of peers. They guessed about half the room noticed; only about a quarter actually did. Everyone is busy in their own spotlight. Comment how many you checked. #psychology #shorts #overthinking #spotlighteffect #socialanxiety",
